{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>For the guilt of the people.</b> That he gave an incorrect ruling, and the people are guilty and all are unintentional. Or the interpretation of לאשמת העם is for the guilt of all human beings, and it is mentioned thus because the priest is the bearer of the Torah and he himself is guarded and holy to the Name." "<b>For his sin.</b> Because of his sin. And since he is great, he offers the bull, which is the greatest of all offerings upon the altar."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:08:32.734913254Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}